      "cluster_id": 0,
      "headline_hint": "Massive unrest and clashes erupt across France as hundreds of thousands protest over living costs",
      "section": "world",
      "batch_position": 0,
      "claim_count": 14,
      "distinct_outlets": 4,
      "source_kinds": {
        "fulltext": 14
      },
      "claims": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "cluster_id": 0,
          "text": "A 19th-century town hall in Limoges, France, was damaged in an apparent arson attack on Saturday following nationwide protests.",
          "kind": "event",
          "outlet": "BBC World",
          "url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/videos/c9dr8kem27zeo?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "cluster_id": 0,
          "text": "Firefighters in Limoges fought the town hall blaze through Saturday night into Sunday morning.",
          "kind": "event",
          "outlet": "BBC World",
          "url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/videos/c9dr8kem27zeo?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "cluster_id": 0,
          "text": "Nationwide cost-of-living protests in France drew an estimated 550,000 demonstrators, according to authorities.",
          "kind": "figure",
          "outlet": "Times of India",
          "url": "https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/those-who-destroyed-must-pay-macrons-warning-to-france-rioters-2400-arrested/articleshow/135036819.cms",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "cluster_id": 0,
          "text": "Unrest across France resulted in the deaths of two people: a 22-year-old police officer struck by a vehicle in Nantes and a protester near Paris.",
          "kind": "event",
          "outlet": "Times of India",
          "url": "https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/those-who-destroyed-must-pay-macrons-warning-to-france-rioters-2400-arrested/articleshow/135036819.cms",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "cluster_id": 0,
          "text": "French authorities reported around 2,400 arrests following nationwide clashes between protesters and police.",
          "kind": "figure",
          "outlet": "Times of India",
          "url": "https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/those-who-destroyed-must-pay-macrons-warning-to-france-rioters-2400-arrested/articleshow/135036819.cms",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "cluster_id": 0,
          "text": "French President Emmanuel Macron stated in a televised address on Sunday: \"Those who destroyed must pay. Those who looted must pay back. Those who sought to bring down the Republic will be held accountable.\"",
          "kind": "quote",
          "outlet": "Times of India",
          "url": "https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/those-who-destroyed-must-pay-macrons-warning-to-france-rioters-2400-arrested/articleshow/135036819.cms",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "cluster_id": 0,
          "text": "French President Emmanuel Macron blamed radical far-left factions and criminal elements for the destruction during the protests.",
          "kind": "event",
          "outlet": "Times of India",
          "url": "https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/those-who-destroyed-must-pay-macrons-warning-to-france-rioters-2400-arrested/articleshow/135036819.cms",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "cluster_id": 0,
          "text": "France's interior ministry reported that almost 1,000 police officers and gendarmes were injured during Saturday's unrest, with seven seriously hurt.",
          "kind": "figure",
          "outlet": "France 24",
          "url": "https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261018-macron-says-nothing-justifies-violence-in-protests-during-address-to-nation",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "cluster_id": 0,
          "text": "French police fired tear gas and stun grenades at hundreds of people gathered at Place de la République in Paris on Sunday.",
          "kind": "event",
          "outlet": "France 24",
          "url": "https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261018-macron-says-nothing-justifies-violence-in-protests-during-address-to-nation",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "cluster_id": 0,
          "text": "Saturday's protests in France brought together trade unions, the anti-Macron Yellow Vests movement, and school students.",
          "kind": "background",
          "outlet": "France 24",
          "url": "https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261018-macron-says-nothing-justifies-violence-in-protests-during-address-to-nation",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "cluster_id": 0,
          "text": "US President Donald Trump posted on social media blaming immigration for the unrest in France, stating \"France is burning!\"",
          "kind": "event",
          "outlet": "France 24",
          "url": "https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261018-macron-says-nothing-justifies-violence-in-protests-during-address-to-nation",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "cluster_id": 0,
          "text": "Protests over cost of living and public services also took place in Spain, Italy, and Portugal.",
          "kind": "event",
          "outlet": "Guardian World",
          "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/18/french-government-crisis-talks-violent-unrest-policing-macron",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "cluster_id": 0,
          "text": "Police in Paris reported a record 855 people were arrested in the French capital alone.",
          "kind": "figure",
          "outlet": "Guardian World",
          "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/18/french-government-crisis-talks-violent-unrest-policing-macron",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "cluster_id": 0,
          "text": "Limoges Mayor Guillaume Guérin stated that municipal police ran out of ammunition around 3:30 p.m. while trying to hold off rioters, calling it a \"colossal failure of the state\".",
          "kind": "event",
          "outlet": "Guardian World",
          "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/18/french-government-crisis-talks-violent-unrest-policing-macron",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cluster_id": 1,
      "headline_hint": "Deadly fire at Canadian military base kills four and injures dozens during training",
      "section": "world",
      "batch_position": 1,
      "claim_count": 12,
      "distinct_outlets": 5,
      "source_kinds": {
        "fulltext": 12
      },
      "claims": [
        {
          "id": 15,
          "cluster_id": 1,
          "text": "A fast-moving fire and subsequent explosion occurred at Canadian Forces Base Wainwright in Alberta during a military training exercise on Saturday.",
          "kind": "event",
          "outlet": "Guardian World",
          "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/18/serious-incident-alberta-military-base-deaths-injuries-canada-carney-cfb-wainwright",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "cluster_id": 1,
          "text": "Four Canadian service members were killed and 39 patients were admitted to hospitals, with at least 19 in critical condition.",
          "kind": "figure",
          "outlet": "Guardian World",
          "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/18/serious-incident-alberta-military-base-deaths-injuries-canada-carney-cfb-wainwright",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "cluster_id": 1,
          "text": "The four deceased service members were identified as Sgt Morgan Wong, Pte Shaun Farrell, Pte Aidan Goulding, and Pte Hayden Lykkemark.",
          "kind": "background",
          "outlet": "Guardian World",
          "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/18/serious-incident-alberta-military-base-deaths-injuries-canada-carney-cfb-wainwright",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "cluster_id": 1,
          "text": "Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney described the incident as \"one of the worst tragedies for the forces on Canadian soil in peacetime.\"",
          "kind": "quote",
          "outlet": "Guardian World",
          "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/18/serious-incident-alberta-military-base-deaths-injuries-canada-carney-cfb-wainwright",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "cluster_id": 1,
          "text": "Prime Minister Mark Carney ordered flags on all federal buildings across Canada to be flown at half-mast.",
          "kind": "event",
          "outlet": "Guardian World",
          "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/18/serious-incident-alberta-military-base-deaths-injuries-canada-carney-cfb-wainwright",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "cluster_id": 1,
          "text": "The Department of National Defence stated there were no indications that the fire at CFB Wainwright was a terrorist attack.",
          "kind": "background",
          "outlet": "Guardian World",
          "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/18/serious-incident-alberta-military-base-deaths-injuries-canada-carney-cfb-wainwright",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "cluster_id": 1,
          "text": "Major-General Wade Rutland stated that soldiers were conducting live-fire combat exercises when a grass fire ignited about 1 km away and shifted towards the administrative area of the range due to uncommonly strong winds.",
          "kind": "event",
          "outlet": "BBC World",
          "url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cxj0ly1m3q81o?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "cluster_id": 1,
          "text": "Alberta's provincial health agency deployed 30 units directly into Wainwright, including 22 ground ambulances, six fixed-wing planes, and two helicopters.",
          "kind": "figure",
          "outlet": "BBC World",
          "url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cxj0ly1m3q81o?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "cluster_id": 1,
          "text": "Canadian Forces Base Wainwright typically has about 690 military personnel and 300 civilian workers on site on a given day.",
          "kind": "background",
          "outlet": "BBC World",
          "url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cxj0ly1m3q81o?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "cluster_id": 1,
          "text": "Military medical personnel parachuted into the town of Wainwright shortly before midnight to help respond to the disaster.",
          "kind": "event",
          "outlet": "Times of India",
          "url": "https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/like-a-war-movie-4-killed-19-critical-after-fire-at-canada-military-base/articleshow/135036349.cms",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "cluster_id": 1,
          "text": "Cathy Keane, an Ontario mayoral candidate, stated on Facebook that her eldest son was among the critically injured military personnel.",
          "kind": "background",
          "outlet": "France 24",
          "url": "https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261018-canada-military-base-fire-four-dead-39-hospitalised",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "cluster_id": 1,
          "text": "Internal military communications indicate that 31 people were very seriously injured in the fire, according to the Globe and Mail.",
          "kind": "figure",
          "outlet": "Channel News Asia",
          "url": "https://www.channelnewsasia.com/world/four-killed-after-high-winds-turn-grass-fire-deadly-canadian-military-base-report-says-6469826",
          "source_kind": "fulltext"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
